r. Characteristics and specification of op amp; Applications of op amp; Block diagram of IC555; Working of IC555. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basic Electronics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A PN junction joins p-type and n-type semiconductor regions. Forward bias lowers the barrier and permits current; reverse bias generally leaves small leakage until breakdown.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Types of semiconductors.; Applications - Diode as rectifier; half wave; full wave and bridge rectifier. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basic Electronics problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

