VALUES (440009352104015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical task in Computer Programming involves this requirement: describe a finite and unambiguous series of steps to transform defined input into output. Explain how Problem solving using flowchart and algorithm applies, outline the main steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical task in Computer Programming involves this requirement: identify the specific purpose or behaviour of History of C in Fundamentals of C. Explain how History of C applies, outline the main steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical task in Computer Programming involves this requirement: select a program branch based on a Boolean condition. Explain how Decision making statements applies, outline the main steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical task in Computer Programming involves this requirement: represent process flow with standard symbols for steps, decisions, input/output and start/end. Explain how Flowchart- Importance of flowchart applies, outline the main steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** An algorithm is a finite sequence of unambiguous steps transforming input to output. It should terminate, be correct and use reasonable time and space.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Flowchart- Importance of flowchart; Symbols of flowchart; how to prepare flowchart; Algorithm design. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking 