odel answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A flowchart represents control flow graphically: oval start/end, rectangle process, parallelogram input/output, diamond decision and arrows.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Problem solving using flowchart and algorithm; Symbols of flowchart; how to prepare flowchart; Algorithm design. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

