arks):** A pointer stores a memory address. Dereferencing accesses the target; pointers should be initialized and used only while valid and correctly typed.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as declaration & initialization of 1-D array; operation in array; String- declaration & initialization; string functions. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

